## 4. YAML endpoint files (under src/main/resources/officefloor/)

`rest/api/owners.POST.yml` defines the ordered create pipeline. Duplicate/identity-relevant steps, in order: `requireEmailDomain` (RequireEmailDomain) → `requirePostcode` → `requireUniqueIdentity` (RequireUniqueIdentity — the 409 check) → ... → `build` → `assignHouseholdId` (AssignHouseholdId) → `countHouseholdMembers` → `capMembershipLevel` → ... → `flagPossibleDuplicate` (FlagPossibleDuplicate — soft match) → `save`. Note `requireUniqueIdentity` and everything after `build` run under `govern: [ transaction ]`, so nothing persists on a 409.

`rest/api/owners/{ownerId}.DELETE.yml` → `load` → `delete` (DeleteOwner, soft delete) → `respond` (RespondWithNoContent).

Escalation mappings:
- `escalation/...DuplicateIdentityException.yml` → `handle: DuplicateIdentityExceptionHandler`
- `escalation/...DisposableEmailDomainException.yml` → `handle: DisposableEmailDomainExceptionHandler`

## 5. Build / test

Maven (with wrapper). Build file: `/home/daniel/sandbox/pom.xml` (artifactId `spring-petclinic-rest`, parent `spring-boot-starter-parent`, using `officefloor-rest-spring-boot-4-starter`). No Gradle files present.

- CI test/build command (`.github/workflows/maven-build-pull-request.yml`): `./mvnw -B verify`
- Master workflow: `./mvnw -B verify org.sonarsource.scanner.maven:sonar-maven-plugin:sonar ...`
- Run app (readme.md): `./mvnw spring-boot:run`
- A single test would be e.g. `./mvnw test -Dtest=AcceptanceTest`.

## Important discrepancy (spec/test vs. implementation)

The acceptance test and OpenAPI/Javadoc disagree with the actual code on what `identityKey` is:

- `AcceptanceTest` asserts `identityKey` matches `[0-9a-f]{64}` (a 64-char lowercase SHA-256 hex) and its comment states the key is `SHA-256 hex over (normalizedTelephone | lowerEmail | soundex(lastName))`.
- The actual `OwnerIdentity.key(...)` returns a **plaintext** `telephone|email|householdId` string (e.g. `+61412345678||A1B2C3D4E5F60718`, per the openapi.yml example), which will **not** match `[0-9a-f]{64}` (it contains `+`, `|`, and uppercase hex). `householdId` is SHA-256 of `lastName|postcode` (uppercase, 12 chars), and **soundex is never used** in production code — the only occurrence of "soundex" is in the test comment. So `coreIdentityKeyIsSha256Hex` would currently fail against this implementation.

